<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="keeper-and-shots" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip files-touched rows and callouts follow the sibling plan fragments' inline markup so the page renders them identically -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">config</span> crates/engine/src/tuning.rs, content/tuning.json</summary><div class="pl-card">A new optional block of shot values: the loft range, the sourced save curve and its fixed quality model, the held share, the parry and block values, the penalty xG, and the three shoot-out values that were hand-set in code. The aim spread, the keeper reach and the xG coefficients are tuned inside their bounds.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>tuning</td><td>+110 / -3</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/shot.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Pure functions: whether a shot's trajectory crosses between the posts under the bar, the shot quality, the save chance on the sourced curve, and the velocity of a parry or a block.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>shot</td><td>+181</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/sim.rs, rules/mod.rs, decision.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">On target is counted at the kick from the trajectory. The keeper attempts a save only on a shot on target, and holds or parries it. A defender near the ball can block once per flight. A parry or a block leaves the defending side as the last touch, so a corner needs a real crossing. Shots can rise over the bar. Penalties and the shoot-out use the same keeper model.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>contest</td><td>+138 / -46</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test-support</span> crates/engine/src/scenario.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A scripted penalty scene and a read of the last touch, for tests only.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>seams</td><td>+25</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/keeper_and_shots.rs and four updated test files</summary><div class="pl-card">Scenes for a wide shot, a shot over the bar, a block, a held save, a parry to a corner and a goal; 500 penalty scenes; slow tests for set pieces from play, an outcome census and the xG refit. Pins for the new values and changed expectations.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>tests</td><td>+480 / -23</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> docs/reference/data-files.md</summary><div class="pl-card">The new tuning rows and a paragraph on on-target, saves, parries and blocks.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>docs</td><td>+25 / -1</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-danger"><strong>The red-card criterion may still fail (high).</strong> On shipped play the keeper arm is 2.67 against 1.64. The cause is how a ten-man side attacks. Implement stops and reports each arm. It never raises a limit.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-danger"><strong>Corners may stay under 3.0 per team (high).</strong> Today there are 0.005. The parry and block values are tuned, and a corner is never scripted.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>The save curve and the xG refit interact (medium).</strong> Saves read a fixed quality model, and the refit comes last.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Every seeded result moves (medium).</strong> Each moved expectation is re-derived and recorded.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Goals leave the band (low).</strong> The product owner accepted this until the final tuning slice.</aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs">
    <summary>Prior revisions (0)</summary>
    <ul><li>No prior revision.</li></ul>
  </details>
